{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/940376-feedback-requested-my-first-attempt-at-a-ready-made-pc","id":940376,"title":"[Feedback Requested] My First Attempt At A Ready Made PC","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-30T18:35:02-07:00","id":940376,"title":"[Feedback Requested] My First Attempt At A Ready Made PC","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Quote:</b> \u201cOh, you think that is weird? Let me tell you about something I saw just last week when I was in the Hedge outside Paris. You won\u2019t believe your ears.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> William Edson was a gifted journalist who was often warned of how his endless curiosity would get him into trouble when he stumbled upon something he was not meant to know. He took this in stride, claiming that if a story existed and it was worth telling, it would be rude to not share with attentive ears. Especially if good money and fame were involved.<br /> <br /> William also had a second job as a writer of mystery novels loosely based on the cases he had investigated, with ambiguous supernatural elements thrown in the background to make the less appealing stories more marketable. He became a best-selling author for quite some time, and just when he thought he had secured a deal to turn one of his books into a movie, he was taken to Arcadia by a True Fae who just so happened to have taken an interest in the art of story-hunting.<br /> <br /> In his Durance, William was forced to hunt for scribbled pages stolen from dreams in a maze-like contraption resembling a typewriter. He would have to overcome many traps and false leads to find these pages filled with pieces of news articles and scientific discoveries that made no sense. Finally, he would take the pages to the exit of the maze, sit down on a desk and write down stories based on the pages so his Keeper could claim them as his own.<br /> <br /> What his Keeper did not expect was that William had the idea of writing a vast mystery novel in the absence of inspirational material from the headlines, and rip it into many pieces to be scattered across the maze. Intrigued by his plaything\u2019s challenge and wanting to prove he was smarter, the Keeper entered the maze and left the exit unguarded.<br /> <br /> When William came back, he discovered that his Fetch had received all the rights to the movie and had become very wealthy. Instead of striking out in rage, William made a bargain. He\u2019d hunt through the Hedge and the Ironside for mysteries both mundane and supernatural to serve as inspiration for the Fetch\u2019s new movies, and William would receive part of profits.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, William lives in his Fetch\u2019s house, which connects to a Hollow that they share. He uses the money he gets from solving cases and the movies to finance his own love of travel, and occasionally help out other changelings in the freehold. He loves hearing people talk about their encounters with strange and mysterious events, and though he offers closure as best as he can, what really motivates him is knowing things no one else could know and living to tell the tale. He is known for offering money and favors in return for leads and other information that might help him in personal and professional investigations, and isn\u2019t shy about poking his nose in dubious places.<br /> <br /> What he does not suspect is that his Fetch is still in contact with his Keeper, because the monster threatens their shared family in nebulous terms. While the Fetch does not plan on sending William back to the Keeper, something very bad might happen if they become enemies and the Fetch decides it\u2019s too risky to keep William around.<br /> <br /> <b>Concept: </b>Mystery Solver/Story Hunter<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> In his Mask, William is a slender but sturdy man in his early thirties with swept back blonde hair and an angular, scholarly face. He has a pointy chin, freckles and some scars on his hands from writing too much with strange tools back in his Durance. His eyes seem to grab details about you that not even you knew about, and he can go on and on about random trivia and travels for hours.<br /> <br /> In his Mien, the left hand has long fingers made of ballpoint pens and skin made of newspaper clippings. On his forehead is a second set of eyes consisting of clicking and whirring investigative tools that resemble magnifying glasses and telescopes. He smells of fresh ink and his steps occasionally sound like a typewriter.<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming: </b>Wizened<br /> <b>Kith: </b>Author + Slewfoot<br /> <b>Mask: </b>Artist<br /> <b>Mien: </b>Scholar<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Journalism) 3, Crafts 1, Computer 1, Medicine 1, Occult (Hedge) 3, Politics 1, Investigation (Rumors &amp; Stories, Body Language) 3, Science 1<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 1, Drive 1, Firearms 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 2, Survival 2, Weaponry 2<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy 2, Expression (Creative Writing) 3, Intimidation 1, Persuasion (Bargaining) 3, Socialize 2, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Journalism, Rumors &amp; Stories), Common Sense, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Academics, Investigation), Eye For The Strange, Good Time Management, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Journalism, Rumors &amp; Stories, Hedge), Investigative Aide (Investigation), Patient, Professional Training 2 (Journalist: Academics, Expression), Professional Training 3 (Detective: Investigation, Survival, Occult), Trained Observer 1, Alternate Identity 2, Allies (Police 2), Contacts (Police, Publishers, Journalists, Lawyers), Fixer, Resources 3, Sympathetic, Dual Kith, Hollow 6 (Luxury Goods 1, Size Matters 1, Escape Route 1, Home Turf 3)<br /> <br /> <b>Health: </b>8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed: </b>10<br /> <b>Clarity: </b>7<br /> <b>Wyrd: </b>2<br /> <br /> <b>Contracts: </b>Bite Of The Wooden Fang, Inanimate Communion 2, Mask Of Superiority 1, Pathfinder, Trivial Reworking, Dreamsteps<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Convince my Fetch I really am his friend, Find a romantic partner and take them on a trip through the Hedge, Earn the enmity or rivalry of an important freehold figure by asking too many questions</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T20:48:56-07:00","id":940426,"title":"","content":"The second Aspiration is two Aspirations folded into one and the third Aspiration is too specific as-worded.<br /> <br /> Are &quot;Bring a romantic partner into the Hedge&quot; and &quot;Attract opposition from a significant freeholder&quot; still in line with the intent of those Aspirations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T20:51:44-07:00","id":940428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/940376-feedback-requested-my-first-attempt-at-a-ready-made-pc?p=940426#post940426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second Aspiration is two Aspirations folded into one and the third Aspiration is too specific as-worded.<br /> <br /> Are &quot;Bring a romantic partner into the Hedge&quot; and &quot;Attract opposition from a significant freeholder&quot; still in line with the intent of those Aspirations?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, those work better.<br /> <br /> What were your general thoughts? Like or dislike?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:13:26-07:00","id":940440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/940376-feedback-requested-my-first-attempt-at-a-ready-made-pc?p=940428#post940428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What were your general thoughts? Like or dislike?</div> </div> </div> </div>The character concept feels like it's trying to do two things at once, the escape seems irrelevant to the seeming as-presented, the dynamic with the fetch is thrown off by the lack of implied differentiation (is the fetch retired or/therefore any worse at investigation and/or writing?), the Skill spread is so eclectic as to seem unfocused, and there's a lot of unnecessary cruft in the Merits.<br /> <br /> There's something there, but a lot of fat-trimming needs done to bring the compelling aspects into focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:23:36-07:00","id":940447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/940376-feedback-requested-my-first-attempt-at-a-ready-made-pc?p=940440#post940440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character concept feels like it's trying to do two things at once, the escape seems irrelevant to the seeming as-presented, the dynamic with the fetch is thrown off by the lack of implied differentiation (is the fetch retired or/therefore any worse at investigation and/or writing?), the Skill spread is so eclectic as to seem unfocused, and there's a lot of unnecessary cruft in the Merits.<br /> <br /> There's something there, but a lot of fat-trimming needs done to bring the compelling aspects into focus.</div> </div> </div> </div> All fair points. Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Do you think I should stick closer to the journalist-as-Slewfoot? The Author Kith does seem a bit superfluous, now that I think about it. Three dots in Expression plus a Specialty is good enough.<br /> <br /> I admit I had a bit of trouble grokking the Wizened method of escape. Do you have any tips on how a Wizened Slewfoot might earn their Seeming?<br /> <br /> The Fetch does need a more solid identity of its own. I'll see what I can about that.<br /> <br /> Anything else?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T22:55:12-07:00","id":940492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/940376-feedback-requested-my-first-attempt-at-a-ready-made-pc?p=940447#post940447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think I should stick closer to the journalist-as-Slewfoot?</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly seems the stronger contrast with the fetch's rich-and-writing-movie-adapted-novels aspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I admit I had a bit of trouble grokking the Wizened method of escape. Do you have any tips on how a Wizened Slewfoot might earn their Seeming? </div> </div> </div>The Wizened hone their selves into an extension of their craft and use their expertise, now unhampered by the interface with Arcadian unreality, to effect their escape.<br /> <br /> A Slewfoot was made what they are as an extension of their capacity to think laterally, draw connections, and decode obscure presentation into clear information.<br /> <br /> Slewfoot Wizened excel at parsing nonsense and wielded that specialty to the end of escaping the thicket of chattering gibberish that defines Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Paradox and other infinite loops are among the archetypal means of navigating past creatures who deal in that ilk, but the nature of the Keeper in relation to Edson is necessarily going to influence the particulars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anything else? </div> </div> </div>The content of the Durance seems a bit thin; weirdly specific events happen in a setup that seems wholly devoted to creating the escape. Consider the Durance and the Keeper as they relate to the wider world.<br /> <br /> Also, is William Courtless?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}